            <ArticleTitle>NbCl5/Zn/PCy3-System-Catalyzed Intramolecular [2 + 2 + 2] Cycloadditions of Diynes and Alkenes To Form Bicyclic Cyclohexadienes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>5398-5401</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b02672</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A NbCl5, Zn, and PCy3 catalytic system that generated low-valent Nb species is used for the synthesis of bicyclic cyclohexadienes from diynes and simple alkenes. A phosphine ligand is important for stabilizing low-valent Nb in the cycloaddition. The bicyclic cyclohexadiene skeleton is important in transition-metal-catalyzed intramolecular cycloadditions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
